# Art: finished drawings from the shelf, named by what they are. `draw` is one line of intent; the server puts the figure's parts on stage
# as ordinary shapes (fox1-tail, kid1-hair), so a label can point at a part and the whole figure can move. pnpm check plays it through
# the server's line path (it needs a shelf), so the parts, the label and the placeholder for a giraffe are looked for on screen.

look paper
scene shelf figure canvas=square lines=2
draw fox1 fox at=27,34 size=46 | sitting, facing left
draw kid1 child at=76,34 size=46 | standing
draw fox2 fox at=27,78 size=30 new | sitting, facing right
draw giraffe1 giraffe at=76,78 size=34
say label near=fox1-tail:below | tail
say | A fox, a child and a smaller fox facing the other way, drawn from the shelf; the giraffe is not on it yet.
wait 1
move kid1 66,34 over=1s
wait 2
